I consider myself a fairly good Nethack player, but I find that I take far 
too long (in terms of turns spent) in each ascension. I believe that my 
fastest game was just under 30,000 turns. I have clocked in ascensions over 
60,000 turns (a weaponless vegan monk-- spent a lot of time getting 
intrinsics and armor).

I believe that my main problem is overpreparing for Gehennom. I don't think 
I've ever stepped foot past the VoTD without at least -30AC. I'm starting to 
think that is overkill. What would be a safe minimum AC to tackle Gehennom 
and beyond?

Also, how do people generally handle stashes? I find myself making an early 
stash, and then having to move my entire stash down to around the level 
before Medusa, which obviously takes a lot of time if I can't find a way to 
levelport.

Do people generally 'j'ump everywhere? I've noticed a few players on NAO 
jumping a lot, which saves a lot of turns. I've actually never really 
considered jumping boots, but they look pretty damn handy on Astral. 
Something to consider, I guess.

Also, does anyone have any general tips for speeding up? It blows my mind 
how people can ascend in 15,000 turns or less. In my current game, I was not 
out of the mines before turn 10,000 (although I did leave with -18 AC).

